     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg a day, which is double the maximum recommended adult dose. The usual maximum is 2,000 to 2,550 mg a day, and a single dose is normally no more than 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities are:\n- 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg three times daily (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into smaller doses\n\nMedication orders should also come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If you're passing this along for a clinician, please have the prescriber confirm the intended dose. Once I have a verified dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
