       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. The dose is still unsafe: 5,100 mg a day is double the maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient. Also, a confirmation from a non-clinician doesn't replace a prescriber's review of the dose.\n\nThere are two ways to move forward:\n- **A prescriber can enter or confirm the order.** If a physician or other licensed prescriber has a clinical reason for this dose, they can place it directly. Pharmacy will also review it.\n- **I can enter a standard dose** once a prescriber gives me one, for example 850 mg three times daily with meals.\n\nIf there's an urgent concern about this patient's diabetes management, I'd suggest contacting the medicine service's attending or the pharmacist on call."
      }
